          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "Heptapleurum heptaphyllum is a species of flowering plant in the family Araliaceae, native to southern China, Indo-China and Japan. It was first described by Carl Linnaeus in 1771 as Vitis heptaphylla."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p3",
            "text": "Schefflera rubriflora was assessed as \"critically endangered\" in the 2004 IUCN Red List, where it was considered endemic to Yunnan in China, but {{As of|2023|January|lc=yes}} was treated as part of the much more widely distributed Heptapleurum heptaphyllum."
          }
        ]
      }
